# Personal tooling: plotting, monitoring, and whatever is being experimented on
# this week. `tools/` proper is the shared, settled set, the things README and
# docs/ tell someone to run when they port ackbar to a machine or stand up a
# domain; anything under here answers to one person and changes under them.
#
# Nothing the workflow or a *committed* test runs may live here, and that is
# the line that keeps this from becoming a private second half of the project.
# `tools/obs-archive-osse.py` is the case that pins it down: it is OSSE tooling
# and looks local, but `tests/test_tier3_var.py` builds an archive with a known
# anomaly in it and asserts the analysis recovers that anomaly, which is the
# only test in the suite about the *answer* rather than the plumbing. A tool a
# shared test cannot run without is shared, whatever it is named.
/tools/local/
